Open role

UI/UX Designer (Product Designer)

San Francisco, CA (On-site)



-  Full-time [data-slot=checkbox-group]]:gap-3 has-[&gt;[data-slot=radio-group]]:gap-3" aria-label="Role summary"&gt;
- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

As a UI/UX Designer, you'll shape the look, feel, and usability of Methodic’s platform (and the white-label apps we offer our clients). You will transform complex financial workflows into intuitive and elegant user interfaces. Working closely with product managers and engineers, you'll ensure that our application is not only powerful in functionality but also easy and even enjoyable to use for both our clients (financial businesses) and their end-users.

Responsibilities

[data-slot=checkbox-group]]:gap-3 has-[&gt;[data-slot=radio-group]]:gap-3 gap-3" aria-label="Role responsibilities"&gt;



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Design user interfaces for the Methodic web application, including dashboards, multi-step workflows (like customer onboarding, account setup), transaction views, reporting pages, and admin tools.



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Create wireframes, high-fidelity mockups, and interactive prototypes that capture both the big-picture flow and the fine-detail interactions of new features.



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Simplify complex processes (such as compliance checks, money transfers, investment operations) into clear, step-by-step user experiences with an emphasis on clarity and usability.



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Establish and maintain a coherent visual style and UI component library (design system) to ensure consistency across the platform and any white-label products.



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Conduct user research and usability testing (when possible) to gather feedback on designs and identify areas of confusion or improvement.



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Iterate on designs based on feedback from users, stakeholders, and analytics (e.g., if users are dropping off at a certain step, refine that screen’s design).



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Collaborate with front-end developers during implementation to ensure design fidelity and that UX considerations are properly addressed (responsive design, accessibility, etc.).

Requirements

[data-slot=checkbox-group]]:gap-3 has-[&gt;[data-slot=radio-group]]:gap-3 gap-3" aria-label="Role requirements"&gt;



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

4+ years of experience in UI/UX or product design with a portfolio of web application designs (bonus points for experience in fintech or other complex, data-heavy apps).



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Proficiency with design and prototyping tools (such as Figma, Sketch, Adobe XD, or similar).



- ]:w-full [&amp;&gt;.sr-only]:w-auto"&gt;

Strong understanding of UX principles and best practices; ability to design for users with varying levels of technical proficiency.

Employer:  Uber Technologies, Inc.

 Job Title:  Product Designer

 Job Location:  San Francisco, California

 Job Type:  Full Time

 Rate of Pay:  $153,000 to $187,000 per year

You will be eligible to participate in Uber's bonus program, and may be offered other types of comp. You will also be eligible for various benefits. More details can be found at the following link https://www.uber.com/careers/benefits .

 Duties:  Responsible for creating intuitive and impactful consumer-facing designs for the Offers team. Lead the design of experiences that connect users with personalized deals, discounts, and promotions, enhancing their journey across Uber products. Craft wireframes, high-quality visuals, conduct user research, and actively shaping the product roadmap. Work closely with Product and Engineering teams to ensure seamless integration across platforms, prioritizing user-centric solutions and measurable outcomes. May telecommute.

Employer will accept a Bachelor's degree in Design, Human-Computer Interaction, Industrial Design, Graphic Design, User Experience Design, Interaction Design, or a related field followed by 5 years of progressive, post-baccalaureate experience in the job offered or in a related occupation.

Position Requires



-  Web and Interface Design; 
-  Web UI; 
-  UX, UE; 
-  Digital design software such as Adobe Creative/Suite/Sketch/Figma; 
-  Information architecture; 
-  User research; 
-  Qualitative and quantitative research; 
-  Drawing and sketching design solutions 

~~ ~~

Company Description CultureFly is a creative company built by pop-culture enthusiasts who design original products for both dedicated and casual fans. The team believes pop culture is a way of living and connecting, and uses this passion to build inclusive communities where everyone can express themselves freely. CultureFly is the creator behind popular subscription boxes such as the Pusheen Box, The Nick Box, and the Star Wars Galaxy Box. Team members collaborate to bring licensed brands and fan-favorite franchises to life through thoughtfully designed collectibles, apparel, home goods, and seasonal items.


Position Summary
We are hiring a Lead Designer to develop Christmas &amp; Seasonal product collections across multiple consumer product categories. This role will manage the day-to-day creative design development from concept through production.
Our ideal candidate has experience building seasonal assortments for Mass Market/Specialty retail, understands how to translate trends into commercially viable products, and can manage multiple categories and timelines simultaneously.&nbsp;&nbsp;Experience in licensed and private branded products is required.


Responsibilities
Design &amp; Creative Development

- Develop seasonal product collections across a wide range of product categories.&nbsp;
- Create original concepts, artwork, packaging, and product direction for holiday programs.&nbsp;
- Build cohesive assortments that support retail strategies and brand positioning.&nbsp;
- Translate trend research into clear product opportunities.&nbsp;
Product Categories

- Home décor – ornaments, garlands, etc.
- Plush &amp; Novelty
- Small soft and hard goods – hydration, accessories, stationery, etc.&nbsp;
- Collectibles&nbsp;
- Outdoor seasonal décor&nbsp;
Trend &amp; Market Research

- Research trends in holiday décor, gifting, color, lifestyle, and retail.&nbsp;
- Analyze market opportunities and competitive assortments.&nbsp;
- Develop trend presentations, mood boards, and seasonal direction.&nbsp;
- Identify opportunities for new product categories and seasonal programs.&nbsp;
Product Development

- Collaborate with Creative Director on product line design and development.&nbsp;
- Prepare design specifications and production-ready files.&nbsp;
- Review samples and prototypes to maintain design accuracy and product quality.&nbsp;
- Manage development timelines and seasonal deadlines.&nbsp;
Team Collaboration

- Manage day-to-day design tasks.
- Participate in creative reviews and product presentations.&nbsp;
- Work cross-functionally with sales, licensing, marketing, and product development teams.&nbsp;
- Present concepts to internal stakeholders.&nbsp;




Qualifications

- 5+ years of experience in product design - Christmas and Seasonal programs for Mass Market/Specialty Retailers.&nbsp;
- Experience designing across multiple consumer product categories.&nbsp;
- Strong understanding of seasonal trends and retail assortments [high/low.]&nbsp;
